# Rust build output
/target
**/target
# A feature named `target` has a proof directory of that name, and it is source
!/docs/examples/**/target
!/tests/hostile/**/target
*.pdb

# Cargo
Cargo.lock.bak

# Novis artifact cache (content-addressed native code; never committed)
/.nvs-cache
*.nvso

# Insta snapshot review leftovers
*.snap.new
*.pending-snap

# Fuzzing
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/corpus
/fuzz/artifacts

# Profiling / benchmark output
/benches/results
perf.data*
flamegraph.svg
*.profraw

# The compose fixtures' CA, copied out of the `certs` volume by the command `tests/db/compose.yaml`'s header names, and named by
# `nvs.toml`'s `[db.main] tls_ca_file`. Remade whenever that volume is, so committing it would
# pin an anchor no server on any other machine holds the key to.
/tests/db/ca.crt

# Editors
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.shared.json
.idea/
*.iml
*.swp
*~

# OS
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local developer config (nvs.toml is server config; keep local overrides out)
/nvs.local.toml
/.env

# Machine-local agent/tool settings
.claude/settings.local.json

# Bytecode from importing a repo script under tools/
__pycache__/

# Unattended loop run artifacts (see docs/agent/coordinator.md). Everything the
# driver writes at run time lives under one directory, so this is one line.
/.loop/

# The CA copied out of the database matrix's containers by a test that wants to
# verify the chain rather than merely encrypt (tests/db/compose.yaml's header).
/tests/db/ca.crt

# The queue `examples/queue-sqlite.nvs` runs against — the one database in this
# repository that is a file rather than a server, named by that fixture's own
# `examples/queue-sqlite.toml` and created by `nvs queue migrate`. It holds
# every job that fixture ever pushed, and a checkout that has never run the
# acceptance sweep has no reason to hold one.
/tests/db/queue-sqlite.db

# Scratch commit-message file (AGENTS.md: a multi-line message goes through a
# file, never an inline `-m`); never part of the tree it describes.
/.agent-tmp/

# The proxied benchmark's two derived inputs (benches/proxied/README.md).
# `.bin/nvs` is a Linux binary staged by `--nvs-bin`, and `generated/pool.conf`
# is rendered from the committed template because php-fpm interpolates no
# environment variable in a pool file. Both are outputs of the tool that reads
# them, and both are digested into every record, so neither is lost by not
# being here.
/benches/proxied/.bin/
/benches/proxied/generated/

# The Docker build context's staged binaries (docs/docker.md § *Building an
# image locally*). `docker/Dockerfile` compiles nothing: the release workflow
# unpacks the published archives into here, so these are release outputs that
# happen to sit in the tree for the length of one build.
/docker/bin/

# The editor clients' package caches and build output. The lockfile IS committed -- `npm ci` needs
# one, and an unpinned tree makes the grammar snapshots reproducible only by luck -- but a session
# that commits `node_modules` is a session whose commit nobody can review. Anchored under
# `editors/` because an unanchored `out/` also swallows website/src/content/docs/docs/core/out/.
/editors/*/node_modules/
/editors/*/out/
/editors/*/.vscode-test/
/editors/*/*.vsix
/editors/*/LICENSE

# The tools' package cache (`bun install`, from the committed `bun.lock`) and `bun nv`'s index,
# `.cache/nv.sqlite`, which is rebuilt from the records under `data/` and never read as a source.
/node_modules/
/.cache/

a.out